__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
# Simulation artifacts. Covers sim/out/ and sim/sim/out/ — the latter is where
# a run from the wrong cwd landed, and it got committed there in 26b0f03 while
# a single-level sim/out/ pattern missed it, so a later run silently rewrote
# committed results. Documented output lives in docs/evaluation/, not here.
sim/**/out/
# Ledger dumps and drill artifacts.
node/out/
# Pilot process logs (node/logs/hub.log and friends) — per-machine noise.
node/logs/

# Per-machine pilot configs (node/INSTALL.md has you cp from *.example.json).
# They carry machine-specific IPs/ports and, once you point at a real model,
# provider endpoints and key-service names. Since 2026-09-22 they also carry
# the `seed` that *is* the identity (agent.js/verifier.js write one back when
# a config file has none), so these files are private keys, not preferences.
node/configs/*.json
!node/configs/*.example.json
# Saved identities that are not .json: the panel launcher's (panel.js) and the
# resident hub's (service/run-hub.sh). Same reason as above — the panel's stake
# and canary record are bound to one, and the other *is* the address everyone
# pins. Pattern rather than two names, so the next one is covered too.
node/configs/.*-seed
